/span></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Further_reading_3\">Further reading</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\" data-nosnippet=\"\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=water&amp;action=edit&amp;section=38\" title=\"Edit section: Further reading\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<ul><li><span class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\">“<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.cnrtl.fr/definition/water\">water</a>”, in <cite><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/fr:Tr%C3%A9sor_de_la_langue_fran%C3%A7aise_informatis%C3%A9\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:fr:Trésor de la langue française informatisé\">Trésor de la langue française informatisé</a></cite> [<cite><span class=\"e-translation\">Digitized Treasury of the French Language</span></cite>], <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">2012</span></span></span></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Hawaiian_Creole\">Hawaiian Creole</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\" data-nosnippet=\"\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=water&amp;action=edit&amp;section=39\" title=\"Edit section: Hawaiian Creole\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_4\">Etymology</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\" data-nosnippet=\"\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=water&amp;action=edit&amp;section=40\" title=\"Edit section: Etymology\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#derived_terms\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">Derived</a> from <span class=\"etyl\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/English_language\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:English language\">English</a></span> <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" href=\"#English\">water</a></i>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Noun_5\">Noun</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\" data-nosnippet=\"\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=water&amp;action=edit&amp;section=41\" title=\"Edit section: Noun\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<p><span class=\"headword-line\"><strong class=\"Latn headword\" lang=\"hwc\">water</strong></span>\n</p>\n<ol><li><span class=\"senseid\" id=\"Hawaiian_Creole:_Q283\" data-lang=\"hwc\" data-id=\"Q283\"><span class=\"usage-label-sense\"><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">(</span><span class=\"ib-content label-content\"><a href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#uncountable\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">uncountable</a></span><span class=\"ib-brac label-brac\">)</span></span> <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\"><a class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" href=\"#English:_Q283\">water</a></span> <span class=\"mention-gloss-paren\">(</span><span class=\"mention-gloss\">an inorganic compound (of molecular formula <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r77195254\"><span class=\"chemf nowrap\">H<sub class=\"template-chem2-sub\">2</sub>O</span>) found at <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/room_temperature#English\" title=\"room temperature\">room temperature</a> and pressure as a clear <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/liquid#English\" title=\"liquid\">liquid</a>; it is present naturally as <a href=\"/wiki/rain#Noun\" title=\"rain\">rain</a>, and found in <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/river#English\" title=\"river\">rivers</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lake#English\" title=\"lake\">lakes</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea#English\" title=\"sea\">seas</a>; its solid form is <a href=\"/wiki/ice#Noun\" title=\"ice\">ice</a> and its gaseous form is <a href=\"/wiki/steam#Noun\" title=\"steam\">steam</a></span><span class=\"mention-gloss-paren\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"HQToggle\" data-nosnippet=\"\" style=\"margin-left: 5px;\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\">quotations&nbsp;▼</a></span><ul class=\"wikt-quote-container\" style=\"display: none;\"><li><div class=\"citation-whole\"><span class=\"cited-source\"><span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\"><b>2000</b></span>, “Matthew 8”, in Joseph Grimes, transl., <cite>Da Jesus Book: Hawaii Pidgin New Testament</cite>‎<sup><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=yKgQAQAAIAAJ\">[5]</a></sup>, Wycliffe Bible Translators, <small><a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-938978-21-3\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0-938978-21-3\">→ISBN</a></small>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://ebible.org/study/content/texts/hwcNT/MT8.html\">page <span class=\"None\" lang=\"und\">110</span></a>:</span><dl><dd><div class=\"h-quotation\"><span class=\"Latn e-quotation cited-passage\" lang=\"hwc\">He tell um, “Go.” So dey wen let go da guys, an go take ova da pigs. An you know wat? All da pigs wen run down one steep hill an fall ova da cliff inside da lake, an drown inside da <b>water</b>.</span><dl><dd><span class=\"e-translation\">And he said unto them, Go. And they came out, and went into the swine: and behold, the whole herd rushed down the steep into the sea, and perished in the <b>waters</b>.</span></dd></dl></div></dd></dl></div></li></ul></li></ol>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Italian\">Italian</h2><span class=\"mw-editsection\" data-nosnippet=\"\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=water&amp;action=edit&amp;section=42\" title=\"Edit section: Italian\"><span>edit</span></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Etymology_5\">Etymology</h3><span class=\"mw-editsection\" data-nosnippet=\"\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"